<!--
  Relay's own launcher mark: the message that arrived, and the answer going
  back. Two bubbles rather than one, because Relay is a conversation and not a
  pile of things shouted at the wearer.
  Nexus renders plugin geometry as stroke only, so the overlap is drawn rather
  than filled: the upper bubble's outline simply stops on both sides of where
  the reply crosses it, which reads as one shape passing in front of the other
  exactly the way a filled gutter would. The gap is a full unit wide, because
  anything tighter closes up on additive optics.
  The tails carry the direction: the upper bubble's sits bottom left, where a
  received message's tail sits in every chat app the wearer already uses, and
  the reply's sits bottom right, where their own outgoing messages live.
  The pair spans nearly the whole 24-unit box on both axes - a mark that reads
  as a conversation needs both halves legible, so neither can be small.
-->
<resources>
    <string-array name="nexus_glyphs">
        <item>relay|M9.6,11.8 L8.4,11.8 L5.4,15.2 L5.4,11.8 L4.4,11.8 A2,2 0 0 1 2.4,9.8 L2.4,4.4 A2,2 0 0 1 4.4,2.4 L13.6,2.4 A2,2 0 0 1 15.6,4.4 L15.6,9.6 M12.6,10.6 L19.6,10.6 A2,2 0 0 1 21.6,12.6 L21.6,16.6 A2,2 0 0 1 19.6,18.6 L19.6,21.8 L16.4,18.6 L12.6,18.6 A2,2 0 0 1 10.6,16.6 L10.6,12.6 A2,2 0 0 1 12.6,10.6 Z</item>
    </string-array>
</resources>
